VERDICT: REJECTED
The task should not be marked complete because the diff includes major out-of-scope and potentially destructive changes beyond project setup.

Critical findings / analysis:
- The working tree contains a massive unrelated rewrite of `.local/skills` and `.local/secondary_skills` (hundreds of files, many deletions). This is not part of “set up imported project” and introduces real risk to agent/tooling behavior; it must be excluded from this task.
- `requirements.txt` was replaced from pinned versions to mostly unpinned package names. That creates non-deterministic installs and can break reproducibility/compatibility across environments. For setup work, dependency constraints should remain stable unless intentionally upgraded and validated.
- `.replit` deployment entrypoint was changed to `python -m daphne ...:8000`, replacing the previous deployment command. This may break deployment assumptions (single exposed app/process and port expectations) and was not validated as part of task #1.
- The core setup intent is partially implemented correctly (dual workflows and `SESSION_SECRET` wiring in Django settings), and `python manage.py check` passes, but the scope/regression issues above are blocking.

Security:
- No serious security violation observed in the reviewed app changes.

Next actions:
1) Revert all unrelated `.local/**` changes and workflow-log churn; submit a minimal, scoped diff for task #1 only.
2) Restore pinned dependency versions (or provide explicit tested upgrades with compatibility proof).
3) Re-validate deployment config separately from dev workflow setup; keep task #1 focused on local run configuration and project initialization.

